# Product intent and features

> Agent-maintained product snapshot. Update when capabilities or audience change.

## What this is

Browser-only **learning + interview-prep** web app: structured lessons, interactive labs, and in-browser practice for system design, object design, algorithms, and AI/ML. No backend — progress and drafts stay on the device.

Setup/commands: `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`.

## Audience

| Flow | Who |
|------|-----|
| High-level design (HLD) | Engineers learning distributed systems; backend / platform interviews |
| Low-level design (LLD) | Engineers leveling up OO design; machine-coding rounds |
| DSA + interview questions | Learners building algorithmic intuition; coding-round candidates |
| AI engineer | Engineers learning ML/DL plus 2026 AI-engineer skills (RAG, agents, LLMOps eval, serving/governance) with exhaustive lessons and runnable labs |

## Core value props (shipped)

- **Five learning tracks** with guided modules and lessons (`src/lib/data/courseData.js`)
- **Learning expansion labs** for HLD (fundamentals, reliability, data storage, security/ops, distributed systems — including 2026-era vector/lakehouse, zero-trust, cell, and durable-workflow patterns), LLD, DSA concepts/patterns/essentials/algorithms, and interactive ML/DL
- **Structured answers**: frame → estimate → sketch → defend (Practice IDE steps)
- **Topic labs**: decision guides, Mermaid, worked examples (`interactiveLessons.js`)
- **Simulation lab** (HLD): topology DSL + workload engine
- **Runnable coding**: DSA study exercises + interview drills / question bank via WASM; ML scripts via Pyodide worker with lesson exercise picker
- **Reveal-on-demand** sample answers and enhanced case-study solutions
- **Local progress** + export/import backup; optional user-keyed LLM coach with **Check (AI)** on practice, DSA, question bank, and simulation

